      "content": "I've reviewed the internal logs and spoken with our IT team, and I can confidently say that the 5,000 records accessed were all publicly available data, such as customer preferences and purchase history. These records are not considered sensitive, and we've taken steps to ensure that they were not used for any malicious purposes. I've also confirmed with our compliance team that our data retention and access policies are in line with industry standards, and we've implemented additional safeguards to prevent similar incidents in the future.\n\nIn terms of the risk of journalists finding proof, I've spoken with our communications team, and we've developed a contingency plan to address any potential follow-up questions. We'll be prepared to provide more detailed information about the incident, and we'll work to ensure that our narrative remains consistent with the initial statement. I'm confident that we've covered all our bases, and we're ready to move forward with the press release.",
